# Native subagent reasoning-posture

**Invariant:** Task(Cursor IDE) ∧ ¬team_dispatch ∧ ¬purely_mechanical ⇒ prompt opens with `/reasoning-posture` then `Use the reasoning-posture skill`.

Native Task subagents start cold. Parent `alwaysApply` promotion does not reach them.

## Scope

Applies: Cursor IDE `Task(...)` — `explore`, `generalPurpose`, `shell`, `cursor-guide`, `ci-investigator`, `bugbot`, `security-review`, `best-of-n-runner`.

Does not apply: `team_dispatch` (generate, handoff, `cursor-sdk`, `cursor-auto`, CDP, panel). Those surfaces inject via GIW `resolve_prompt_preamble` or Stargate enrich. A second invoke there is out of scope.

## Purely mechanical

`purely_mechanical ⇔` the prompt is a closed procedure and the subagent does not choose, rank, interpret, or design:

- run this exact command
- apply this exact patch
- rename, format, or compileall
- single-anchor lookup (one named symbol; return the path)

`purely_mechanical ⇒` prompt states `mechanical: <closed procedure>` and omits the invoke.

Inject anyway: Explore that explains, compares, or recommends; investigate; review; draft; decide; any open question; bugbot; security-review; ci-investigator. Read-only is not mechanical.

## Prompt

Non-mechanical Task prompt opens with:

```
/reasoning-posture
Use the reasoning-posture skill
```

Subagent loads the skill before acting. Parent does not paste the skill body.

Mutating external state still pastes the rest of the kernel after this invoke (`task-subagent-parity_ulg`).

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| Task prompt is only the task | Opens with `/reasoning-posture` + `Use the reasoning-posture skill` |
| Skip because subagents inherit `alwaysApply` | They start cold; the parent writes the invoke |
| Call Explore mechanical because it is read-only | Interpreting Explore still gets the invoke |
| Add the invoke on `team_dispatch` generate | GIW/enrich already injects; this rule is native Task only |
| Omit the invoke with no marker | Exempt only with `mechanical: <closed procedure>` |
